    {
      "id": "WoRsb5cokvBAbuDLMovJY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13373.418990090991,
      "y": 701.5645179101122,
      "width": 3736.4545174748077,
      "height": 3975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 850648690,
      "version": 166,
      "versionNonce": 563994098,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788156307440,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yes. For your 3-person team, feature-wise division is actually better because everyone can work across the same codebase while owning a clear feature.\n\nI would divide your SIH project like this:\n\nPerson 1 — AI / Vehicle Intelligence\n\nOwns:\n\n1. Camera/Video Input\n\n\n2. Vehicle Detection — YOLO\n\n\n3. Vehicle Tracking — ByteTrack/BoT-SORT\n\n\n4. ANPR / OCR\n\n\n5. Vehicle Re-ID / Embeddings\n\n\n6. Detection Event Generation\n\n\n7. AI → Backend integration\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nVideo → Vehicle → Plate → Embedding → Detection Event\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 2 — Backend / Intelligence\n\nOwns:\n\n1. API layer\n\n\n2. Database\n\n\n3. Vehicle Identity Management\n\n\n4. Cross-Camera Matching\n\n\n5. Trajectory Reconstruction\n\n\n6. Camera & Location Management\n\n\n7. Traffic Analytics\n\n\n8. Authentication & Authorization\n\n\n9. Real-time WebSocket layer\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nEvents → Global Vehicle ID → Trajectory → Analytics\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 3 — Frontend / Visualization\n\nOwns:\n\n1. Dashboard UI\n\n\n2. GIS Map\n\n\n3. Vehicle Search\n\n\n4. Vehicle Details\n\n\n5. Individual Vehicle Trajectory\n\n\n6. Camera Visualization\n\n\n7. Real-Time Traffic Dashboard\n\n\n8. Traffic Heatmap/Congestion\n\n\n9. Charts & Analytics\n\n\n10. Public/Authorized views\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nBackend Data → Map + Dashboard + Real-Time Visualization\n\n\n---\n\nBut there's one important thing\n\nDon't make the boundaries hard.\n\nFor example, Person 1 owns ANPR, but Person 2 needs to understand the ANPR output.\n\nSo use this structure:\n\nSHARED CONTRACT\n                         │\n          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐\n          ↓              ↓              ↓\n       PERSON 1       PERSON 2       PERSON 3\n         AI          BACKEND         FRONTEND\n          │              │              │\n          │              │              │\n     Detection ───────→ Events ───────→ UI\n     Embedding ───────→ Matching\n     Plate ───────────→ Identity\n                       Trajectory ───→ Map\n                       Analytics ────→ Dashboard\n\nMost important division\n\nDon't divide:\n\n> \"You write these files, you write those files.\"\n\n\n\nDivide:\n\n> \"You own this feature from implementation → testing → integration.\"\n\n\n\nThat's much more professional.\n\nFor example, Person 2 owns Cross-Camera Matching. They can modify whatever backend files are necessary to make that feature work, while Person 1 provides the embeddings and Person 3 visualizes the result.\n\nAnd before coding, you should define the API/data contract between these features so nobody has to wait for another person to finish.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yes. For your 3-person team, feature-wise division is actually better because everyone can work across the same codebase while owning a clear feature.\n\nI would divide your SIH project like this:\n\nPerson 1 — AI / Vehicle Intelligence\n\nOwns:\n\n1. Camera/Video Input\n\n\n2. Vehicle Detection — YOLO\n\n\n3. Vehicle Tracking — ByteTrack/BoT-SORT\n\n\n4. ANPR / OCR\n\n\n5. Vehicle Re-ID / Embeddings\n\n\n6. Detection Event Generation\n\n\n7. AI → Backend integration\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nVideo → Vehicle → Plate → Embedding → Detection Event\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 2 — Backend / Intelligence\n\nOwns:\n\n1. API layer\n\n\n2. Database\n\n\n3. Vehicle Identity Management\n\n\n4. Cross-Camera Matching\n\n\n5. Trajectory Reconstruction\n\n\n6. Camera & Location Management\n\n\n7. Traffic Analytics\n\n\n8. Authentication & Authorization\n\n\n9. Real-time WebSocket layer\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nEvents → Global Vehicle ID → Trajectory → Analytics\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 3 — Frontend / Visualization\n\nOwns:\n\n1. Dashboard UI\n\n\n2. GIS Map\n\n\n3. Vehicle Search\n\n\n4. Vehicle Details\n\n\n5. Individual Vehicle Trajectory\n\n\n6. Camera Visualization\n\n\n7. Real-Time Traffic Dashboard\n\n\n8. Traffic Heatmap/Congestion\n\n\n9. Charts & Analytics\n\n\n10. Public/Authorized views\n\n\n\nMain responsibility:\n\nBackend Data → Map + Dashboard + Real-Time Visualization\n\n\n---\n\nBut there's one important thing\n\nDon't make the boundaries hard.\n\nFor example, Person 1 owns ANPR, but Person 2 needs to understand the ANPR output.\n\nSo use this structure:\n\nSHARED CONTRACT\n                         │\n          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐\n          ↓              ↓              ↓\n       PERSON 1       PERSON 2       PERSON 3\n         AI          BACKEND         FRONTEND\n          │              │              │\n          │              │              │\n     Detection ───────→ Events ───────→ UI\n     Embedding ───────→ Matching\n     Plate ───────────→ Identity\n                       Trajectory ───→ Map\n                       Analytics ────→ Dashboard\n\nMost important division\n\nDon't divide:\n\n> \"You write these files, you write those files.\"\n\n\n\nDivide:\n\n> \"You own this feature from implementation → testing → integration.\"\n\n\n\nThat's much more professional.\n\nFor example, Person 2 owns Cross-Camera Matching. They can modify whatever backend files are necessary to make that feature work, while Person 1 provides the embeddings and Person 3 visualizes the result.\n\nAnd before coding, you should define the API/data contract between these features so nobody has to wait for another person to finish.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NZDMWluK9UU5Zb7KtQcSM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12764.200730005994,
      "y": 884.4623240731678,
      "width": 8,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
