    {
      "id": "9TqjIBUX5J1DBN5qMouHt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -11881.079125021177,
      "y": -1739.6808683730776,
      "width": 2032.1097412109375,
      "height": 4500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 35174318,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 283497710,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788158144458,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yes. For 4 people, I’d divide it into 4 feature ownership areas, not 4 repositories.\n\nPerson 1 — Computer Vision / Camera Pipeline\n\nOwns the entire vehicle-perception pipeline:\n\nCamera/RTSP/video input\n\nOpenCV\n\nYOLO vehicle detection\n\nByteTrack / BoT-SORT tracking\n\nVehicle classification\n\nBounding boxes\n\nLocal vehicle IDs\n\nFrame preprocessing\n\nAI performance/FPS\n\nDetection event generation\n\n\nOutput:\n\nCamera → Detection → Tracking → Local Vehicle Event\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 2 — ANPR + Vehicle Re-ID\n\nOwns vehicle identity intelligence:\n\nLicense-plate detection\n\nOCR / ANPR\n\nPlate preprocessing\n\nOCR confidence\n\nPlate correction/fuzzy matching\n\nVehicle embedding generation\n\nVehicle Re-ID\n\nEmbedding similarity\n\nCross-camera matching logic\n\nGlobal Vehicle ID\n\n\nOutput:\n\nDetection → Plate + Embedding → Global Vehicle Identity\n\nThis person works closely with Person 1 because the AI pipeline produces the vehicle images/tracks they need.\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 3 — Backend + Database + Trajectory\n\nOwns the system's core intelligence/data layer:\n\nFastAPI\n\nAPI implementation\n\nPostgreSQL\n\nPostGIS\n\nRedis if needed\n\nDetection-event storage\n\nCamera management\n\nVehicle records\n\nCross-camera event storage\n\nTrajectory reconstruction\n\nRoute/camera graph\n\nVehicle history\n\nAuthentication & authorization\n\n\nOutput:\n\nAI Events → Database → Global Vehicle → Trajectory ,[geoJSON]\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 4 — Frontend + GIS + Traffic Analytics\n\nOwns everything the user sees:\n\nReact + TypeScript\n\nMapLibre\n\nPublic dashboard\n\nAuthorized dashboard\n\nVehicle search\n\nVehicle details\n\nIndividual trajectory visualization\n\nCamera visualization\n\nTraffic heatmap\n\nCongestion visualization\n\nTraffic charts\n\nReal-time updates\n\nWebSocket frontend integration\n\n\nOutput:\n\nBackend → Map + Dashboard + Real-Time Visualization\n\n\n---\n\nThe overall division\n\nPERSON 1\nCAMERA + DETECTION + TRACKING\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 2\nANPR + OCR + RE-ID + GLOBAL ID\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 3\nBACKEND + DATABASE + TRAJECTORY\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 4\nGIS + DASHBOARD + TRAFFIC ANALYTICS\n\nBut don't make these isolated.\n\nThe important shared contracts are:\n\nP1 → P2\nVehicle Track Data\n\nP2 → P3\nVehicle Identity / Detection Event\n\nP3 → P4\nVehicle + Trajectory + Traffic APIs\n\nP3 ↔ P4\nReal-time WebSocket\n\nAnd everyone shares responsibility for testing and integration.\n\nFor your SIH project, this is a much better 4-person division because each person has a complete feature area, while the interfaces between them remain clearly defined.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yes. For 4 people, I’d divide it into 4 feature ownership areas, not 4 repositories.\n\nPerson 1 — Computer Vision / Camera Pipeline\n\nOwns the entire vehicle-perception pipeline:\n\nCamera/RTSP/video input\n\nOpenCV\n\nYOLO vehicle detection\n\nByteTrack / BoT-SORT tracking\n\nVehicle classification\n\nBounding boxes\n\nLocal vehicle IDs\n\nFrame preprocessing\n\nAI performance/FPS\n\nDetection event generation\n\n\nOutput:\n\nCamera → Detection → Tracking → Local Vehicle Event\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 2 — ANPR + Vehicle Re-ID\n\nOwns vehicle identity intelligence:\n\nLicense-plate detection\n\nOCR / ANPR\n\nPlate preprocessing\n\nOCR confidence\n\nPlate correction/fuzzy matching\n\nVehicle embedding generation\n\nVehicle Re-ID\n\nEmbedding similarity\n\nCross-camera matching logic\n\nGlobal Vehicle ID\n\n\nOutput:\n\nDetection → Plate + Embedding → Global Vehicle Identity\n\nThis person works closely with Person 1 because the AI pipeline produces the vehicle images/tracks they need.\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 3 — Backend + Database + Trajectory\n\nOwns the system's core intelligence/data layer:\n\nFastAPI\n\nAPI implementation\n\nPostgreSQL\n\nPostGIS\n\nRedis if needed\n\nDetection-event storage\n\nCamera management\n\nVehicle records\n\nCross-camera event storage\n\nTrajectory reconstruction\n\nRoute/camera graph\n\nVehicle history\n\nAuthentication & authorization\n\n\nOutput:\n\nAI Events → Database → Global Vehicle → Trajectory ,[geoJSON]\n\n\n---\n\nPerson 4 — Frontend + GIS + Traffic Analytics\n\nOwns everything the user sees:\n\nReact + TypeScript\n\nMapLibre\n\nPublic dashboard\n\nAuthorized dashboard\n\nVehicle search\n\nVehicle details\n\nIndividual trajectory visualization\n\nCamera visualization\n\nTraffic heatmap\n\nCongestion visualization\n\nTraffic charts\n\nReal-time updates\n\nWebSocket frontend integration\n\n\nOutput:\n\nBackend → Map + Dashboard + Real-Time Visualization\n\n\n---\n\nThe overall division\n\nPERSON 1\nCAMERA + DETECTION + TRACKING\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 2\nANPR + OCR + RE-ID + GLOBAL ID\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 3\nBACKEND + DATABASE + TRAJECTORY\n              │\n              ↓\nPERSON 4\nGIS + DASHBOARD + TRAFFIC ANALYTICS\n\nBut don't make these isolated.\n\nThe important shared contracts are:\n\nP1 → P2\nVehicle Track Data\n\nP2 → P3\nVehicle Identity / Detection Event\n\nP3 → P4\nVehicle + Trajectory + Traffic APIs\n\nP3 ↔ P4\nReal-time WebSocket\n\nAnd everyone shares responsibility for testing and integration.\n\nFor your SIH project, this is a much better 4-person division because each person has a complete feature area, while the interfaces between them remain clearly defined.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
